{
  "id": "bruce-effect",
  "term": "Bruce effect",
  "definition": "The Bruce effect is a phenomenon in which early pregnancy may be interrupted when a recently mated female is exposed to an unfamiliar male. In mice, this depends on a mating-related memory of the original male and the female’s ability to tell his odor apart from the odor of a novel male.",
